create-overview

This command maps and analyzes the design and functionality of the target codebase.

## Step 1:
Give me a high-level overview of this repository. Starting at the top level of the repo.
I want you to identify the primary components of the system. Determine what it is meant to do, how it does it.
Identify common patterns used in the repo. Identify the main services and describe what they do.
Create an architecture diagram of the repo.

Once you have completed this, save your findings to a file named 'HIGH_LEVEL_OVERVIEW.md'

## Step 2:
Once you have finished this and saved the file, I want you to dig into each one of the components that you identified for this codebase, and perform a detailed, granular analysis for each one. Collate this more granular investigation back into the initial high level review you made. Do this for every component/subsystem/service you can identify.

Create a comprehensive plan for the codebase review to ensure you don't skip any files or folders. You can skip build output directories and files. 

Once you have built a plan, execute the review step by step. 

## Step 3:
Save the findings of this codebase analysis to a markdown file in the root of the repo, named 'ARCHITECTURE.md’.
This should be a comprehensive, verbose artifact of all aspects of this analysis.
This should have a consistent structure for all services and components.
Include relevant diagrams and also include a simple ascii tree diagram of the repo structure and the intended functionality of code in subfolders.
Do not skip any folders.
